<graph edgedefault="undirected"><node id="ADP 3-90">
  <data key="d0">ADP 3-90</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">ADP 3-90 is a military doctrine publication dated 31 July 2019 that outlines tactical fundamentals and the science of tactics.&lt;SEP&gt;ADP 3-90 is a document dated 31 July 2019 discussing tactical fundamentals.&lt;SEP&gt;ADP 3-90 is the primary publication for the offense and defense at the tactical level, providing authoritative guidance.&lt;SEP&gt;ADP 3-90 is the manual containing the text regarding tactics, operations, and risk.&lt;SEP&gt;A doctrinal publication dated 31 July 2019 containing tactical fundamentals and risk reduction factors.&lt;SEP&gt;ADP 3-90 is a document containing doctrine regarding command and the operations process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64802ecdf1ea6ab74a5fb1338e603319&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6888ee0fc5990f7bfbc04bd6cfb28c44</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ADP 3-0">
  <data key="d0">ADP 3-0</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">ADP 3-0 is a referenced military doctrine publication that defines combined arms and combat power.&lt;SEP&gt;ADP 3-0 defines defeat as rendering a force incapable of achieving its objectives.&lt;SEP&gt;ADP 3-0 is referenced for discussions on strategic and operational levels and the definition of defeat.&lt;SEP&gt;ADP 3-0 provides additional information on the consolidation of gains.&lt;SEP&gt;ADP 3-0 provides information on irregular warfare and distinguishes it from conventional warfare.&lt;SEP&gt;A referenced document providing information on Army tenets of operations and principles of war.&lt;SEP&gt;ADP 3-0 is a referenced document providing further details on the imperatives of Army operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6888ee0fc5990f7bfbc04bd6cfb28c44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cd5b0031ce939f299628087297273c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dc5bd4d34c1ec405578b6459e4d25c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83b849ddc9c6eed87498b4d0cd5715fc</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759217</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Army">
  <data key="d0">Army</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Army is the military organization that collectively describes warfighting functions and trains leaders for tactical situations.&lt;SEP&gt;Army forces operate in more than just the land domain and depend on affecting enemy behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;The Army utilizes capabilities and doctrines such as ADP 3-90 for tactical operations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Army is a military branch whose involvement in counterterrorism is limited by Department of Defense directives.&lt;SEP&gt;The Army follows an organizational approach for multidomain operations and joint operations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Army is a military organization that utilizes imperatives to align efforts and maintain advantage over adversaries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6888ee0fc5990f7bfbc04bd6cfb28c44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb8968defc8aab21974e71c786c3b7a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b8ed0cc5c4a8e919c8f12065962561e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dc5bd4d34c1ec405578b6459e4d25c4</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Science of Tactics">
  <data key="d0">Science of Tactics</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The science of tactics involves understanding measurable military aspects like capabilities, techniques, and procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;The science of tactics is the understanding of military aspects that can be measured and codified.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combined Arms">
  <data key="d0">Combined Arms</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Combined arms refers to the synchronized and simultaneous application of arms to achieve an effect greater than separate use.&lt;SEP&gt;Combined arms advantages are exploited to the maximum possible extent in hasty operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748533</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combined Arms Team">
  <data key="d0">Combined Arms Team</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A combined arms team is a formation that uses combined arms through synchronized application of elements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748534</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combat Power">
  <data key="d0">Combat Power</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Combat power is the total means of destructive, constructive, and information capabilities a unit can apply at a given time.&lt;SEP&gt;Combat power is concentrated at the decisive point to place an enemy in a disadvantageous position.&lt;SEP&gt;The capability of friendly forces that commanders seek to preserve and concentrate against enemy vulnerabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748534</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Warfighting Functions">
  <data key="d0">Warfighting Functions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Warfighting functions are the last six elements of combat power described by the Army.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748534</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Leaders">
  <data key="d0">Leaders</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Leaders train for tactical situations, master the science of tactics, and develop decision-making abilities through education and experience.&lt;SEP&gt;Leaders need creativity and clarity to make decisions under uncertainty and act decisively.&lt;SEP&gt;Leaders require critical skills in tactics and understanding commander's intent.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748534</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Commanders">
  <data key="d0">Commanders</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Commanders are leaders responsible for defeating adversary forces and accomplishing missions that support operational or strategic purposes. They apply principles and imperatives to achieve objectives, developing operations and selecting how to employ force discriminately. Their actions are considered strategic, operational, or tactical based on whether they achieve corresponding objectives. To succeed, Commanders apply tactics, balance risk, and maintain initiative, seeking to initiate combat on favorable terms.

Commanders are responsible for maintaining momentum and making critical decisions while training subordinates in tactical operations. They must weigh information, uncertainty, risk, and available forces against the disposition of the main body to achieve their purpose. Additionally, Commanders face specific challenges in enabling collaboration and assuring access within contested environments. Through these multifaceted responsibilities, they strive to fulfill their role in achieving objectives and defeating enemies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64802ecdf1ea6ab74a5fb1338e603319&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6888ee0fc5990f7bfbc04bd6cfb28c44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3a8a845280b83251233809b74dd7287&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b8ed0cc5c4a8e919c8f12065962561e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dc5bd4d34c1ec405578b6459e4d25c4</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759268</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enemy Forces">
  <data key="d0">Enemy Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Enemy forces are opposing units whose decision-making abilities commanders seek to disrupt and degrade.&lt;SEP&gt;Enemy forces are opposing groups with goals that commanders seek to defeat.&lt;SEP&gt;Enemy forces are opposing forces that tacticians develop solutions against.&lt;SEP&gt;Enemy forces are opposed by commanders and create uncertainty in the operational environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Hostile groups establishing positions and ambush sites in urban areas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6888ee0fc5990f7bfbc04bd6cfb28c44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0e9849c17fc43c6ff4116d537e8d8ae</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778752897</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Friendly Forces">
  <data key="d0">Friendly Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Friendly Forces encompass military units, personnel, capabilities, organizations, and materiel operating under command to seize the initiative. These forces are protected and sustained by commanders during and after battles, requiring agility, protection, and responsive support throughout operations. Success for Friendly Forces is determined by winning battles based on the outcomes of engagements, necessitating a robust structure capable of facing complex threats from opposing forces.

Coordination is vital, as Friendly Forces are managed by commanders who facilitate information sharing through the operations process. Military personnel within these groups require synchronization and communication to maintain effectiveness. Specific operational safety protocols dictate that personnel must be alerted of impending dangers by aircraft. Furthermore, in complex settings such as urban environments, Friendly Forces employ SUAS operations to navigate threats and maintain operational advantage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6888ee0fc5990f7bfbc04bd6cfb28c44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0e9849c17fc43c6ff4116d537e8d8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-466f239ae26f543930ce42fb131832cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3a8a845280b83251233809b74dd7287</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778752929</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Initiative">
  <data key="d0">Initiative</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Initiative allows commanders to make the enemy react and maintain control over the tempo of operations.&lt;SEP&gt;The initiative is a key operational state that friendly forces seek to seize, retain, and exploit against enemy forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748534</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Momentum">
  <data key="d0">Momentum</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Momentum complements initiative and reflects a unit's combat power and operational tempo.&lt;SEP&gt;Momentum complements and helps maintain the initiative, reflecting a unit's combat power and operational tempo.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748534</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Offensive Action">
  <data key="d0">Offensive Action</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Offensive action is key to achieving decisive results and is normally required for tactical success.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748534</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decisive Results">
  <data key="d0">Decisive Results</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Decisive results are the outcome achieved through offensive action and accomplishing missions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748534</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="31 July 2019">
  <data key="d0">31 July 2019</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">31 July 2019 is the publication date associated with ADP 3-90.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64802ecdf1ea6ab74a5fb1338e603319</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748534</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Course of Action">
  <data key="d0">Course of Action</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A course of action (COA) is developed to address specific tactical problems and represents a choice among options.&lt;SEP&gt;A plan or option evaluated by commanders, where the best COA may involve the greatest risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748534</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rules of Engagement">
  <data key="d0">Rules of Engagement</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Regulations that impose constraints on friendly and enemy force capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748534</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Terrain">
  <data key="d0">Terrain</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Physical ground that leaders learn to employ to their advantage and commanders seek to control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748534</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Limit of Advance">
  <data key="d0">Limit of Advance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific point where offensive action ends when forces reach it.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748534</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Leadership">
  <data key="d0">Leadership</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">One of the eight elements of combat power.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748534</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Information">
  <data key="d0">Information</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">One of the eight elements of combat power.&lt;SEP&gt;Current and accurate data accessed by systems to support commander understanding and decision-making.&lt;SEP&gt;Information is a factor continually weighed by Commanders alongside uncertainty and risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64802ecdf1ea6ab74a5fb1338e603319&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748534</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
