</node>
<node id="Information Operations">
  <data key="d0">Information Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Information operations are effectively integrated by friendly forces to influence relevant actors.&lt;SEP&gt;Activities conducted to isolate and degrade enemy decision-making abilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cyberspace Operations">
  <data key="d0">Cyberspace Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cyberspace operations are capabilities integrated by friendly forces to affect enemy capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Activities conducted to isolate and degrade enemy decision-making abilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Electronic Warfare">
  <data key="d0">Electronic Warfare</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Electronic warfare capabilities are integrated by friendly forces to the lowest possible echelons.&lt;SEP&gt;Activities conducted to isolate and degrade enemy decision-making abilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Soldiers">
  <data key="d0">Soldiers</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Soldiers are affected by the emotional and physical aspects of combat, including fatigue and fear.&lt;SEP&gt;Soldiers are affected by the effects of combat, which leaders must understand.&lt;SEP&gt;Soldiers require patience when achieving operational and theater strategic objectives.&lt;SEP&gt;Soldiers are individuals in the Army who must understand political implications and prioritize ethical conduct.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6888ee0fc5990f7bfbc04bd6cfb28c44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b8ed0cc5c4a8e919c8f12065962561e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dc5bd4d34c1ec405578b6459e4d25c4</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759229</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Liaison Officers">
  <data key="d0">Liaison Officers</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Liaison officers are used to accelerate the planning process alongside collaborative systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Staffs">
  <data key="d0">Staffs</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Staffs provide input to commanders and assist in the military decision-making process.&lt;SEP&gt;Staffs advise Commanders in determining optimal formation and organization.&lt;SEP&gt;Staffs work with commanders to synchronize capabilities in congested cyberspace and electromagnetic environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Staffs work with commanders when planning special operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64802ecdf1ea6ab74a5fb1338e603319&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3a8a845280b83251233809b74dd7287&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b8ed0cc5c4a8e919c8f12065962561e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759230</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ADP 6-0">
  <data key="d0">ADP 6-0</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">ADP 6-0 defines situational understanding as the product of applying analysis and judgment.&lt;SEP&gt;ADP 6-0 contains a discussion of the mission variables known as METT-TC.&lt;SEP&gt;ADP 6-0 contains a description of the operations process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6888ee0fc5990f7bfbc04bd6cfb28c44</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combat">
  <data key="d0">Combat</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Combat is a lethal clash of opposing wills and a violent struggle characterized by friction, violence, and chance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tactics">
  <data key="d0">Tactics</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tactics involves the art and science of military aspects like capabilities, techniques, and procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;Tactics is the employment, ordered arrangement, and directed actions of forces in relation to each other.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6888ee0fc5990f7bfbc04bd6cfb28c44</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Art of Tactics">
  <data key="d0">Art of Tactics</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The art of tactics includes innovative application of means, decision making under uncertainty, and understanding combat effects on soldiers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mission Variables">
  <data key="d0">Mission Variables</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mission variables have many combinations that make each tactical situation unique and are analyzed for situational understanding.&lt;SEP&gt;Mission variables are collected by commanders to make informed decisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Information Environment">
  <data key="d0">Information Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The information environment affects actors and military operations and requires understanding to influence behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Land Domain">
  <data key="d0">Land Domain</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tactical through strategic land operations depend on the ability of Army forces to affect behavior in this domain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Military Decision-Making Process">
  <data key="d0">Military Decision-Making Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Commanders and staffs need to master the fundamentals of this process before abbreviating it.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Area of Operations">
  <data key="d0">Area of Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The area of operations (AO) is the specific region where Army forces affect the behavior and capabilities of enemies and populations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Local Population">
  <data key="d0">Local Population</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The local population is one of the relevant actors whose behavior and capabilities Army forces seek to affect in the area of operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adversaries">
  <data key="d0">Adversaries</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Adversaries are distinct from enemy forces and are among the actors whose behavior is affected by Army operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Opposing forces employing various weapon systems in urban environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0e9849c17fc43c6ff4116d537e8d8ae</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778752897</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Warning Orders">
  <data key="d0">Warning Orders</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Warning orders are used by units to maximize parallel planning and share information with subordinates early.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Collaborative Systems">
  <data key="d0">Collaborative Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Collaborative systems are tools used alongside liaison officers to accelerate the military decision-making process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unit Cohesion">
  <data key="d0">Unit Cohesion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Unit cohesion is a critical factor that leaders must protect against the risk of collapse due to combat stress.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Risk">
  <data key="d0">Risk</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Risk characterizes all operations involving choices and the cost of those choices.&lt;SEP&gt;Risk is a necessary element in formulating and executing plans, often embraced as opportunity by successful commanders.&lt;SEP&gt;The exposure of someone or something valued to danger, harm, or loss, inherent in every military decision.&lt;SEP&gt;Risk is a factor assessed continuously by Commanders and balanced against opportunities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64802ecdf1ea6ab74a5fb1338e603319&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resources">
  <data key="d0">Resources</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Resources are allocated by commanders as part of the forces and control measures in operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Resources are allocated by Commanders to minimize risk through changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64802ecdf1ea6ab74a5fb1338e603319</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Control Measures">
  <data key="d0">Control Measures</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Control measures are arranged and chosen by commanders to manage forces and operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tempo">
  <data key="d0">Tempo</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tempo refers to the speed or rhythm of the operation which commanders seek to control.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tactical Fundamentals">
  <data key="d0">Tactical Fundamentals</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tactical Fundamentals is the section title covering the art and science of tactics in ADP 3-90.&lt;SEP&gt;A section within ADP 3-90 discussing risk reduction, command decisions, and operational agility.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Main Body">
  <data key="d0">Main Body</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The principal part of a tactical command or formation, excluding detached elements like guards.&lt;SEP&gt;The Main Body is the principal part of a tactical command or formation, excluding detached elements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64802ecdf1ea6ab74a5fb1338e603319&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tactical Command">
  <data key="d0">Tactical Command</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The overall command structure of which the main body is the principal part.&lt;SEP&gt;A Tactical Command is a structure of which the Main Body is the principal part.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64802ecdf1ea6ab74a5fb1338e603319&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Formation">
  <data key="d0">Formation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Formation is a military organization structure of which the Main Body is the principal part.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64802ecdf1ea6ab74a5fb1338e603319</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Advance Guards">
  <data key="d0">Advance Guards</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Detached elements of a command excluded from the main body during tactical operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Advance Guards are detached elements of a command not included in the Main Body.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64802ecdf1ea6ab74a5fb1338e603319&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flank Guards">
  <data key="d0">Flank Guards</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Detached elements of a command excluded from the main body during tactical operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Flank Guards are detached elements of a command not included in the Main Body.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64802ecdf1ea6ab74a5fb1338e603319&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Covering Forces">
  <data key="d0">Covering Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Detached elements of a command excluded from the main body during tactical operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Covering Forces are detached elements of a command not included in the Main Body.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64802ecdf1ea6ab74a5fb1338e603319&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reserves">
  <data key="d0">Reserves</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reserves are forces whose size is weighed by Commanders against the disposition of the Main Body.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64802ecdf1ea6ab74a5fb1338e603319</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security Forces">
  <data key="d0">Security Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Security Forces are forces whose size is weighed by Commanders against the disposition of the Main Body.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64802ecdf1ea6ab74a5fb1338e603319</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Uncertainty">
  <data key="d0">Uncertainty</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A degree of unknown factors inherent in decisions that contributes to risk and requires acceptance by commanders.&lt;SEP&gt;Uncertainty is a factor continually weighed by Commanders alongside information and risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Uncertainty characterizes tactical operations and requires commanders to balance risks with opportunities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64802ecdf1ea6ab74a5fb1338e603319&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Task Organization">
  <data key="d0">Task Organization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Task Organization is an element subject to changes as part of the Operations Process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64802ecdf1ea6ab74a5fb1338e603319</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mission">
  <data key="d0">Mission</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mission is a specific objective for which Commanders determine optimal formation and organization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64802ecdf1ea6ab74a5fb1338e603319</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Priorities">
  <data key="d0">Priorities</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Priorities are an element subject to changes as part of the Operations Process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64802ecdf1ea6ab74a5fb1338e603319</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Operations Process">
  <data key="d0">Operations Process</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The operations process helps commanders drive operations and develop a common operational picture.&lt;SEP&gt;The Operations Process includes changes to task organization, mission, and priorities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64802ecdf1ea6ab74a5fb1338e603319&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Opportunities">
  <data key="d0">Opportunities</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Opportunities are potential benefits associated with changes, balanced against risks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64802ecdf1ea6ab74a5fb1338e603319</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Detached Elements">
  <data key="d0">Detached Elements</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Detached Elements are parts of a command, such as advance guards, that are not included in the Main Body.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64802ecdf1ea6ab74a5fb1338e603319</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Purpose">
  <data key="d0">Purpose</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Purpose is the objective Commanders aim to achieve by balancing opportunities and risks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64802ecdf1ea6ab74a5fb1338e603319</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Situation">
  <data key="d0">Situation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Situation is the context that warrants changes and resource allocation by Commanders.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64802ecdf1ea6ab74a5fb1338e603319</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chapter 1">
  <data key="d0">Chapter 1</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Chapter 1 is a section of the ADP 3-90 document containing the provided doctrine.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64802ecdf1ea6ab74a5fb1338e603319</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Operational Environment">
  <data key="d0">Operational Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A thorough understanding of the operational environment helps commanders develop tactical solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Operational Environment encompasses the political, military, economic, social, and other variables influencing operations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Operational Environment is the context commanders must understand to achieve objectives and defeat adversary forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b8ed0cc5c4a8e919c8f12065962561e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dc5bd4d34c1ec405578b6459e4d25c4</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759229</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consolidate Gains">
  <data key="d0">Consolidate Gains</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Consolidate gains involves activities to make enduring any temporary operational success and set conditions for sustainable security.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subordinate Leaders">
  <data key="d0">Subordinate Leaders</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Subordinate leaders execute the commander's plan and require training to master tactics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hasty Operation">
  <data key="d0">Hasty Operation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A hasty operation directs immediately available forces using fragmentary orders with minimal preparation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="9th Armored Division">
  <data key="d0">9th Armored Division</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The 9th Armored Division conducted the seizure of the bridge at Remagen in March 1945.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bridge At Remagen">
  <data key="d0">Bridge At Remagen</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The bridge at Remagen was seized by the 9th Armored Division during a hasty operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seizure Of The Bridge At Remagen">
  <data key="d0">Seizure Of The Bridge At Remagen</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The seizure of the bridge at Remagen illustrates a hasty operation conducted in March 1945.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deliberate Operation">
  <data key="d0">Deliberate Operation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A deliberate operation allows the development and coordination of detailed plans including multiple branches and sequels.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="1st Infantry Division">
  <data key="d0">1st Infantry Division</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The 1st Infantry Division conducted a breaching operation during Operation Desert Storm.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Breaching Operation">
  <data key="d0">Breaching Operation</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The breaching operation during the opening hours of the ground phase of Operation Desert Storm illustrates a deliberate operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Operation Desert Storm">
  <data key="d0">Operation Desert Storm</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Operation Desert Storm included a ground phase in February 1991 where deliberate operations occurred.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combat Information">
  <data key="d0">Combat Information</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Combat information is unevaluated data gathered by or provided directly to the tactical commander.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tactical Intelligence">
  <data key="d0">Tactical Intelligence</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Tactical intelligence requirements may not be satisfied in time due to the perishable nature of combat information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="JP 2-01">
  <data key="d0">JP 2-01</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">JP 2-01 defines combat information as unevaluated data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intelligence Staff">
  <data key="d0">Intelligence Staff</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The intelligence staff helps commanders assess combat information used in decision making.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fragmentary Orders">
  <data key="d0">Fragmentary Orders</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Fragmentary orders are used in hasty operations to direct immediately available forces with minimal preparation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Common Operational Picture">
  <data key="d0">Common Operational Picture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The common operational picture is developed by the operations process to facilitate decision making and communication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Planning Process">
  <data key="d0">Planning Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The planning process prepares branches or sequels and helps commanders resource operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decision-making Process">
  <data key="d0">Decision-making Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The decision-making process must not be paralyzed by a lack of information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748538</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Legitimate Authorities">
  <data key="d0">Legitimate Authorities</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Legitimate authorities receive transition of control after consolidating gains.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748538</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Higher Commander">
  <data key="d0">Higher Commander</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A superior leader whose intent and constraints guide the commander's decision-making process.&lt;SEP&gt;The higher commander sets intent and constraints that guide decision making.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748538</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unit">
  <data key="d0">Unit</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A unit's combat power and tempo are reflected by momentum.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748538</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Commander">
  <data key="d0">Commander</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Leaders responsible for making informed decisions, managing risk, and shaping success in military operations.&lt;SEP&gt;The commander whose intent and ROE understanding is imperative for mission planning and operations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commander receives situational understanding and support from Civil Affairs forces and operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-466f239ae26f543930ce42fb131832cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-416988242ce00406b1b8539639cba1d3</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759224</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enemy">
  <data key="d0">Enemy</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The opposing force whose weaknesses commanders seek to expose and whose preparations impact operational timing.&lt;SEP&gt;The enemy utilizes urban terrain for cover and employs various surface-to-air attacks against friendly aircraft.&lt;SEP&gt;The Enemy is an opposing force whose proximity to friendly forces complicates airspace planning.&lt;SEP&gt;Opposing force that may observe landing zones and engage aircraft.&lt;SEP&gt;Enemy forces may observe suitable Landing Zones and engage in activity near interchanges.&lt;SEP&gt;The Enemy is denied opportunities for exploitation through military government operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-255d2259beb766bee7c72c77afa91c9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-466f239ae26f543930ce42fb131832cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3a8a845280b83251233809b74dd7287&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf2865a0fcb23cc7955b08ca1d4c5b89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-416988242ce00406b1b8539639cba1d3</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN34839-ATP_3-06.1-000-WEB-1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759224</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decision">
  <data key="d0">Decision</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Choices made by commanders that include risk and determine the course of action within intent and constraints.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748538</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Operation">
  <data key="d0">Operation</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Military activities where risk cannot be avoided and must be managed to accomplish the mission.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748538</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battalion Task Force">
  <data key="d0">Battalion Task Force</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A tactical unit example that can conduct actions on contact without the loss of momentum.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748538</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Actions On Contact">
  <data key="d0">Actions On Contact</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A series of combat actions taken on contact with the enemy to develop the situation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748538</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Course Of Action">
  <data key="d0">Course Of Action</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A plan or option commanders consider regarding risk to the force and mission against perceived benefits.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748538</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security Elements">
  <data key="d0">Security Elements</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Units occupying security areas to provide early warning, protection, and initial enemy contact.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748538</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reserve">
  <data key="d0">Reserve</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Forces kept available to compensate for increased risk or exploit opportunities during operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748538</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mission Command Approach">
  <data key="d0">Mission Command Approach</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A method used by friendly forces to achieve agility through shared understanding and estimates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748538</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Information Technologies">
  <data key="d0">Information Technologies</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Systems integrated with leaders and formations to reduce risk and facilitate decisive action.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748538</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subordinates">
  <data key="d0">Subordinates</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Personnel who collaborate with commanders to analyze risk levels and determine mitigation strategies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748538</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security Area">
  <data key="d0">Security Area</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">An area occupied by a unit's security elements including the areas of influence of those elements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748538</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Agility">
  <data key="d0">Agility</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The ability of friendly forces to react faster than enemy forces, mitigating risk in tactical operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778748538</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Planning">
  <data key="d0">Planning</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Situational understanding and running estimates that reduce risk and inform bold decisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3d34db12b1eccda9d78d171ad5c4a96</data>
