</node>
<node id="Department Of State">
  <data key="d0">Department Of State</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Department Of State is a federal agency mentioned in relation to leading agency societies and referenced in JP 3-26.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb8968defc8aab21974e71c786c3b7a9</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Department Of Defense">
  <data key="d0">Department Of Defense</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Department Of Defense issues directives that limit Army involvement in counterterrorism and conducts activities outside the United States.&lt;SEP&gt;The Department of Defense establishes counterproliferation policy and works with USSOCOM on weapons of mass destruction efforts.&lt;SEP&gt;The U.S. government department responsible for security cooperations and force assistance activities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb8968defc8aab21974e71c786c3b7a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cd5b0031ce939f299628087297273c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe9b99ab479688bf15c5eb6b71313a3b</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Direct Action">
  <data key="d0">Direct Action</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Direct Action is a specific activity conducted by Army Special Operations Forces.&lt;SEP&gt;Direct action is an assigned special operations activity conducted by special operations forces.&lt;SEP&gt;Direct Action consists of high-risk, low-visibility short-duration strikes and small-scale offensive actions defined in JP 3-05.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb8968defc8aab21974e71c786c3b7a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-416988242ce00406b1b8539639cba1d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83b849ddc9c6eed87498b4d0cd5715fc</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Foreign Internal Defense">
  <data key="d0">Foreign Internal Defense</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Foreign Internal Defense is a specific activity conducted by Army Special Operations Forces.&lt;SEP&gt;Foreign internal defense is an assigned special operations activity conducted by special operations forces.&lt;SEP&gt;Foreign Internal Defense involves activities to assist a partner government in addressing internal threats and is defined in JP 3-22.&lt;SEP&gt;Activities that overlap with security force assistance to build host-nation capacity against threats.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb8968defc8aab21974e71c786c3b7a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cd5b0031ce939f299628087297273c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-416988242ce00406b1b8539639cba1d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83b849ddc9c6eed87498b4d0cd5715fc</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Foreign Humanitarian Assistance">
  <data key="d0">Foreign Humanitarian Assistance</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Foreign humanitarian assistance is an assigned special operations activity conducted by special operations forces.&lt;SEP&gt;Foreign Humanitarian Assistance is limited in scope and duration to relieve human suffering and is defined in JP 3-29.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb8968defc8aab21974e71c786c3b7a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83b849ddc9c6eed87498b4d0cd5715fc</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Civil Affairs Operations">
  <data key="d0">Civil Affairs Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Civil Affairs Operations are executed through four core competencies to support commanders and integrate civil knowledge.&lt;SEP&gt;Civil affairs operations are an assigned special operations activity executed through core competencies like civil network development.&lt;SEP&gt;Civil Affairs Operations are activities conducted by Army special operations forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb8968defc8aab21974e71c786c3b7a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-416988242ce00406b1b8539639cba1d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83b849ddc9c6eed87498b4d0cd5715fc</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Special Forces">
  <data key="d0">Special Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Special Forces are units that employ infantry tactics and conduct direct action operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Special Forces units lived and worked with partners in the Philippines as part of JSOTF-P special operations activities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb8968defc8aab21974e71c786c3b7a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f9296b5d072caec55997f55d6e957ea</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ranger Units">
  <data key="d0">Ranger Units</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Ranger Units are units that employ infantry tactics and conduct direct action operations alongside Special Forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb8968defc8aab21974e71c786c3b7a9</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Civil Affairs Units">
  <data key="d0">Civil Affairs Units</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Civil Affairs Units can establish civil-military operations centers to coordinate partner institutions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb8968defc8aab21974e71c786c3b7a9</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="528th Sustainment Brigade">
  <data key="d0">528th Sustainment Brigade</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The 528th Sustainment Brigade provides temporary support to humanitarian assistance efforts and enables international organizations.&lt;SEP&gt;528th Sustainment Brigade provides planners integrated into a Special Forces group planning team.&lt;SEP&gt;The 528th Sustainment Brigade is one of the only Army special operations forces elements capable of providing Role 2 level care.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb8968defc8aab21974e71c786c3b7a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5c39d7c4f2e0018da66a43c03ab90bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b8ed0cc5c4a8e919c8f12065962561e</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Civil-Military Operations Center">
  <data key="d0">Civil-Military Operations Center</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Civil-Military Operations Center coordinates partner institutions and gathers information to prioritize restoring basic services.&lt;SEP&gt;A civil-military operations center is a mechanism established by Civil Affairs forces to coordinate activities and share information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb8968defc8aab21974e71c786c3b7a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-416988242ce00406b1b8539639cba1d3</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joint Special Operations Task Force-Philippines">
  <data key="d0">Joint Special Operations Task Force-Philippines</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Joint Special Operations Task Force-Philippines (JSOTF-P) was established in 2002 to advise and assist the Armed Forces of the Philippines in combating terrorist groups.&lt;SEP&gt;The Joint Special Operations Task Force-Philippines was established in 2002 as part of broader U.S. efforts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb8968defc8aab21974e71c786c3b7a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f9296b5d072caec55997f55d6e957ea</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="United States">
  <data key="d0">United States</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The United States established JSOTF-P as part of the Global War on Terror and maintains a partnership with the Philippines.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States is the country where Department of Defense activities are conducted outside of for humanitarian assistance.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States is a nation whose military forces and partners engage in unconventional warfare and special operations.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States is the country whose interests are impacted by threats and protected by security cooperations.&lt;SEP&gt;The nation whose security interests and foreign policy are supported by security cooperations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb8968defc8aab21974e71c786c3b7a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cd5b0031ce939f299628087297273c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f9296b5d072caec55997f55d6e957ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe9b99ab479688bf15c5eb6b71313a3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8f143cf228a70fcc3b24d3886031aa2</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Philippines">
  <data key="d0">Philippines</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Philippines is the host nation where JSOTF-P operated and where the Comprehensive Agreement on Bangsamoro was implemented.&lt;SEP&gt;The Philippines is the location associated with the Joint Special Operations Task Force.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb8968defc8aab21974e71c786c3b7a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f9296b5d072caec55997f55d6e957ea</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759214</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="JP 3-26">
  <data key="d0">JP 3-26</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">JP 3-26 is a publication referencing the Department of Justice and Department of State.&lt;SEP&gt;JP 3-26 is a joint publication referenced in relation to counterterrorism definitions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb8968defc8aab21974e71c786c3b7a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-416988242ce00406b1b8539639cba1d3</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759215</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="JP 3-05">
  <data key="d0">JP 3-05</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">JP 3-05 is a document referenced for the definition of special reconnaissance.&lt;SEP&gt;JP 3-05 is a publication defining Direct Action operations.&lt;SEP&gt;JP 3-05 is a joint publication defining unconventional warfare.&lt;SEP&gt;JP 3-05 is a joint publication referenced regarding hostage rescue and operational preparation of the environment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb8968defc8aab21974e71c786c3b7a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f9296b5d072caec55997f55d6e957ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe9b99ab479688bf15c5eb6b71313a3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8f143cf228a70fcc3b24d3886031aa2</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759215</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="JP 3-29">
  <data key="d0">JP 3-29</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">JP 3-29 is a publication defining Foreign Humanitarian Assistance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb8968defc8aab21974e71c786c3b7a9</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759215</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="JP 3-22">
  <data key="d0">JP 3-22</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">JP 3-22 is a publication defining Foreign Internal Defense.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb8968defc8aab21974e71c786c3b7a9</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759215</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ATP 3-05.2">
  <data key="d0">ATP 3-05.2</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">ATP 3-05.2 provides details on how Army forces enable host nation forces to maintain internal stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb8968defc8aab21974e71c786c3b7a9</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759215</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Counterterrorism">
  <data key="d0">Counterterrorism</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Counterterrorism involves activities to neutralize terrorists and their networks to prevent violence and coercion.&lt;SEP&gt;Counterterrorism is an assigned special operations activity conducted by special operations forces.&lt;SEP&gt;Counterterrorism is an area where Army involvement is limited by Department of Defense directives.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb8968defc8aab21974e71c786c3b7a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-416988242ce00406b1b8539639cba1d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83b849ddc9c6eed87498b4d0cd5715fc</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759215</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Internal Stability">
  <data key="d0">Internal Stability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Internal Stability is a goal enabled by Army special operations forces within host nations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb8968defc8aab21974e71c786c3b7a9</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759215</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Host Nation">
  <data key="d0">Host Nation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Host Nation refers to the partner government or country receiving assistance or defense support.&lt;SEP&gt;The host nation whose forces are enabled by Army forces to maintain internal stability.&lt;SEP&gt;The target nation where security force assistance operations are conducted to develop capability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb8968defc8aab21974e71c786c3b7a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cd5b0031ce939f299628087297273c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f9296b5d072caec55997f55d6e957ea</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759215</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hostage Rescue And Recovery">
  <data key="d0">Hostage Rescue And Recovery</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
