<node id="Army Special Operations Forces">
  <data key="d0">Army Special Operations Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Army Special Operations Forces are specialized military units designed for irregular warfare and precise employment rather than mass deployment. These forces operate with a long-term perspective, executing missions with precision while acknowledging inherent limitations. Partnership, integration, and persistence serve as the foundational principles for their operations, which are planned and executed to support broader campaign plans.

The organization conducts a diverse range of specific activities, including civil affairs, direct action, counterterrorism support, foreign internal defense, and foreign humanitarian assistance. They are heavily involved in security cooperation and personnel recovery activities. To succeed in these missions, Army Special Operations Forces require the ability to penetrate enemy systems to conduct hostage rescue and other critical operations.

In terms of specific regional engagement, Army Special Operations Forces continue to support the Philippines with exercises and operations following the deactivation of JSOTF-P. This ongoing support exemplifies their commitment to sustained security cooperation and operational persistence in key strategic areas.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb8968defc8aab21974e71c786c3b7a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cd5b0031ce939f299628087297273c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f9296b5d072caec55997f55d6e957ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5c39d7c4f2e0018da66a43c03ab90bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-416988242ce00406b1b8539639cba1d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8f143cf228a70fcc3b24d3886031aa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b8ed0cc5c4a8e919c8f12065962561e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dc5bd4d34c1ec405578b6459e4d25c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83b849ddc9c6eed87498b4d0cd5715fc</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759250</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FM 3-05">
  <data key="d0">FM 3-05</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">FM 3-05 is a United States Army field manual and publication dated 26 June 2025. Titled Army Special Operations Activities, the document serves as the primary source outlining doctrine related to Army Special Operations activities. It encompasses a broad range of military topics, including unconventional warfare, special operations principles, and civil affairs operations. The manual details the fundamentals and limitations of Army special operations forces, establishing the foundational knowledge required for these units.

The publication is organized into chapters, with Chapter 2 specifically outlining Army special operations activities. Beyond structural details, FM 3-05 contains doctrine on Army special operations principles as well as Army and Special Operations imperatives, providing guidance on operational conduct. Additionally, the field manual document contains references to events involving the Ranger company, integrating specific operational examples or historical contexts within its doctrinal framework. Through these components, FM 3-05 functions as a comprehensive guide for the forces it governs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb8968defc8aab21974e71c786c3b7a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cd5b0031ce939f299628087297273c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f9296b5d072caec55997f55d6e957ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5c39d7c4f2e0018da66a43c03ab90bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-416988242ce00406b1b8539639cba1d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe9b99ab479688bf15c5eb6b71313a3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8f143cf228a70fcc3b24d3886031aa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db557cf9378c4bf4f84c616fc05e03ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b8ed0cc5c4a8e919c8f12065962561e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dc5bd4d34c1ec405578b6459e4d25c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83b849ddc9c6eed87498b4d0cd5715fc</data>
  <data key="d4">D:\Academic resources\ARN44116-FM_3-05-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1778759282</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
