  <data key="d12">1778748553</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Commanders" target="Initiative">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Commanders maintain the initiative to enable friendly forces to disrupt enemy decision making.</data>
  <data key="d9">control,maintenance</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82</data>
  <data key="d11">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1778748540</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Commanders" target="Enemy Forces">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Commanders seek to disrupt enemy decision making and destroy critical capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Commanders strive to defeat enemy forces to accomplish missions.&lt;SEP&gt;Commanders act against enemy forces and assess their situation to accomplish missions.</data>
  <data key="d9">adversarial,defeat,disruption,opposition</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d11">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1778748541</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Commanders" target="Friendly Forces">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Commanders are responsible for sustaining and protecting subordinate friendly forces.&lt;SEP&gt;Commanders control friendly forces and allocate resources to achieve objectives.&lt;SEP&gt;Commanders communicate decisions and information between friendly forces.</data>
  <data key="d9">command,communication,control,leadership,protection,sustainment</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-52b99141c5846e6f7e60bd1665d2ca82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e26474dd179be588057ca7d29d2fdfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eca3fafdc38ef10f3b3cf3553129b6b</data>
  <data key="d11">D:\Academic resources\ARN34828-ADP_3-90-000-WEB-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1778748541</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Commanders" target="Course of Action">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Commanders develop a course of action to address specific tactical problems.&lt;SEP&gt;Commanders evaluate courses of action, noting the best may involve the greatest risk.</data>
